{
  "note": "Which tagged place picture (art/backdrops/manifest.json) shows what a person is doing in the bench. Keys are core act ids; '@home', '@workplace' and '@target' resolve from the person's records; a list is tried in order until one has a picture. Organization classifications map to data/content/place-kinds.json business kinds when their suffix is not already one. filingOffices maps the office GOV names as taking a contest's filings (case-insensitive pattern on its name) to its picture; filingClerkOfficeKinds are the offices whose holder, if they live in town, is the clerk at the counter. sceneSettings maps a story scene's setting kind (OPUS-PEOPLE's composeScene) to its pictures; '@org' is the setting record's organization. situationPlaces picks a picture by the story situation and its setting (first one painted wins; @home is the person's own dwelling); schoolPlacesByAge picks a school picture by the person's age. electionNight is the results sheet's picture: where a candidate watches returns, and where a voter voted.",
